{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "google-drive-cdn-worker-api",
		"name": "Google Drive CDN Worker API",
		"description": "# 🚀 Google Drive CDN Worker API\n\nTransform your Google Drive into a lightning-fast global CDN using Cloudflare Workers.\n\n## 🔐 Authentication\n\nAll API endpoints (except public file access and stats) require authentication using one of these methods:\n\n1. **Bearer Token**: `Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_TOKEN`\n2. **API Key Header**: `x-api-key: YOUR_API_TOKEN`\n\n## 📝 Setup Instructions\n\n1. Set the `{{baseUrl}}` variable to your worker URL (e.g., `https://your-worker.workers.dev`)\n2. Set the `{{apiToken}}` variable to your API token\n3. Start making requests!\n\n## 📚 Available Endpoints\n\n- **POST /api/files** - Upload files (multipart, max 20MB)\n- **POST /api/uploads** - Initialize resumable upload for large files\n- **GET /api/files/{id}** - Get file metadata\n- **DELETE /api/files/{id}** - Delete a file\n- **GET /files/{id}** - Public file access (no auth required)\n- **GET /api/stats** - Get service statistics\n- **GET /api/dashboard/summary** - Get dashboard summary\n- **GET /api/dashboard/files** - List files with pagination\n\n## 🎯 Features\n\n- ✅ Direct multipart upload (up to 20MB)\n- ✅ Resumable uploads for large files\n- ✅ File metadata management\n- ✅ Public CDN URLs\n- ✅ Video streaming with Range support\n- ✅ Statistics tracking\n- ✅ File filtering and pagination",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
		"version": "3.0.0"
	},
	"auth": {
		"type": "bearer",
		"bearer": [
			{
				"key": "token",
				"value": "{{apiToken}}",
				"type": "string"
			}
		]
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Files",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Upload File (Multipart)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"// Save file ID for later use",
									"if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
									"    const response = pm.response.json();",
									"    if (response.data && response.data.id) {",
									"        pm.environment.set('fileId', response.data.id);",
									"        pm.environment.set('cdnUrl', response.data.rawUrl);",
									"        console.log('File uploaded successfully!');",
									"        console.log('File ID:', response.data.id);",
									"        console.log('CDN URL:', response.data.rawUrl);",
									"    }",
									"}"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [],
						"body": {
							"mode": "formdata",
							"formdata": [
								{
									"key": "file",
									"type": "file",
									"src": [],
									"description": "Select the file to upload (max 20MB)"
								},
								{
									"key": "metadata",
									"value": "{\n  \"name\": \"my-image.jpg\",\n  \"description\": \"Uploaded via Postman\",\n  \"parents\": [\"root\"]\n}",
									"type": "text",
									"description": "Optional JSON metadata for the file"
								}
							]
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/files",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"files"
							]
						},
						"description": "Upload a file directly using multipart/form-data.\n\n**Maximum file size: 20MB**\n\nFor larger files, use the `/api/uploads` endpoint for resumable uploads.\n\n### Request Body\n\n- `file` (required): The file to upload\n- `metadata` (optional): JSON string with file metadata\n  - `name`: Custom filename\n  - `description`: File description\n  - `parents`: Array of parent folder IDs (default: [\"root\"])\n\n### Response\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"id\": \"1abc123xyz\",\n    \"name\": \"my-image.jpg\",\n    \"mimeType\": \"image/jpeg\",\n    \"size\": \"524288\",\n    \"rawUrl\": \"https://your-worker.workers.dev/files/1abc123xyz\"\n  }\n}\n```"
					},
					"response": [
						{
							"name": "Success - File Uploaded",
							"originalRequest": {
								"method": "POST",
								"header": [],
								"body": {
									"mode": "formdata",
									"formdata": [
										{
											"key": "file",
											"type": "file",
											"src": "example.jpg"
										},
										{
											"key": "metadata",
											"value": "{\"name\":\"example.jpg\",\"description\":\"Test upload\"}",
											"type": "text"
										}
									]
								},
								"url": {
									"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/files",
									"host": [
										"{{baseUrl}}"
									],
									"path": [
										"api",
										"files"
									]
								}
							},
							"status": "Created",
							"code": 201,
							"_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
							"header": [
								{
									"key": "Content-Type",
									"value": "application/json"
								}
							],
							"body": "{\n    \"status\": \"success\",\n    \"data\": {\n        \"id\": \"1abc123xyz\",\n        \"name\": \"example.jpg\",\n        \"mimeType\": \"image/jpeg\",\n        \"size\": \"524288\",\n        \"rawUrl\": \"https://your-worker.workers.dev/files/1abc123xyz\"\n    }\n}"
						},
						{
							"name": "Error - File Too Large",
							"originalRequest": {
								"method": "POST",
								"header": [],
								"body": {
									"mode": "formdata",
									"formdata": [
										{
											"key": "file",
											"type": "file",
											"src": "large-file.mp4"
										}
									]
								},
								"url": {
									"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/files",
									"host": [
										"{{baseUrl}}"
									],
									"path": [
										"api",
										"files"
									]
								}
							},
							"status": "Payload Too Large",
							"code": 413,
							"_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
							"header": [
								{
									"key": "Content-Type",
									"value": "application/json"
								}
							],
							"body": "{\n    \"status\": \"error\",\n    \"error\": {\n        \"code\": \"payload_too_large\",\n        \"message\": \"file exceeds 20971520 bytes, use /api/uploads\"\n    }\n}"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Initialize Resumable Upload",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"// Save upload session details",
									"if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
									"    const response = pm.response.json();",
									"    if (response.data && response.data.uploadSession) {",
									"        pm.environment.set('uploadUrl', response.data.uploadSession.uploadUrl);",
									"        pm.environment.set('uploadId', response.data.uploadSession.uploadId);",
									"        pm.environment.set('fileId', response.data.uploadSession.fileId);",
									"        console.log('Upload session created!');",
									"        console.log('Upload URL:', response.data.uploadSession.uploadUrl);",
									"        console.log('Upload ID:', response.data.uploadSession.uploadId);",
									"    }",
									"}"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"large-video.mp4\",\n  \"mimeType\": \"video/mp4\",\n  \"size\": 104857600,\n  \"description\": \"Large video file\",\n  \"parents\": [\"root\"]\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/uploads",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"uploads"
							]
						},
						"description": "Create a resumable upload session for large files (> 20MB).\n\nThis endpoint returns an `uploadUrl` that you can use to stream file chunks directly to Google Drive.\n\n### Request Body\n\n- `name` (required): File name\n- `mimeType` (optional): MIME type (e.g., \"video/mp4\")\n- `size` (optional): File size in bytes\n- `description` (optional): File description\n- `parents` (optional): Array of parent folder IDs\n\n### Response\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"uploadSession\": {\n      \"uploadUrl\": \"https://www.googleapis.com/upload/drive/v3/files?uploadType=resumable&upload_id=xyz\",\n      \"uploadId\": \"xyz\",\n      \"fileId\": \"1abc123\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Next Steps\n\nUse the returned `uploadUrl` to upload your file chunks:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X PUT \"{{uploadUrl}}\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: video/mp4\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Range: bytes 0-524287/104857600\" \\\n  --data-binary @chunk1.bin\n```"
					},
					"response": [
						{
							"name": "Success - Session Created",
							"originalRequest": {
								"method": "POST",
								"header": [
									{
										"key": "Content-Type",
										"value": "application/json"
									}
								],
								"body": {
									"mode": "raw",
									"raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"large-video.mp4\",\n  \"mimeType\": \"video/mp4\",\n  \"size\": 104857600\n}"
								},
								"url": {
									"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/uploads",
									"host": [
										"{{baseUrl}}"
									],
									"path": [
										"api",
										"uploads"
									]
								}
							},
							"status": "Created",
							"code": 201,
							"_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
							"header": [
								{
									"key": "Content-Type",
									"value": "application/json"
								}
							],
							"body": "{\n    \"status\": \"success\",\n    \"data\": {\n        \"uploadSession\": {\n            \"uploadUrl\": \"https://www.googleapis.com/upload/drive/v3/files?uploadType=resumable&upload_id=xyz123\",\n            \"uploadId\": \"xyz123\",\n            \"fileId\": \"1abc123xyz\"\n        }\n    }\n}"
						}
					]
				},
				{
